# Lies you're told (docs/DIALOGUE.md, "Lies you're told"). A line ending in ~lie:<key> is a lie the
# player hears (heard_lie:<key>); a line ending in ~truth:<key> is the truth (knows:<key>). Once a
# player has both, the choice with `callout <key>` shows, tagged [Evidence]. Nobody is punished for
# believing a lie: the truth opens a better answer, and that's the payoff.

conv wanderer.scavenger.chemist
for wanderer:scavenger
when !nmem:sold_chemist
topic "Ask if anywhere's worth looking."
prio world
voice plain

node start
  say "The chemist's in {here}. Back room, top shelf. Nobody's touched it. Clean as a whistle." ~lie:scav.chemist
  say "Bit of food and it's yours. The knowing, I mean. The shelf's free."
  > @buy Give him a tin. -> sold   cost item:food*1   do nset:sold_chemist; later:6h:scav.came_back
  > @hunter "That door was forced. Boot marks." -> caught_out   if bg:hunter,police
  > @catch "Picked clean on Day 3. I asked." -> caught_out   callout scav.chemist
  > @no "Not today." -> hub

node sold
  say "Pleasure. Mind how you go. I mean that part."
  > @back1 "Something else." -> hub

node caught_out
  say "All right, all right. Picked clean. But the vet's on the south road still has bandages. Honest. That one's free, for the cheek."
  do nset:honest
  > @back2 "Something else." -> hub

conv wanderer.scavenger.came_back
for wanderer:scavenger
when due:scav.came_back & !nmem:honest
once
greet
voice plain

node start
  say "You're back. Did you go to the chemist's? Don't tell me. I can see it on you. Still here, though. That's the main thing."

conv wanderer.doctor.chemist
for wanderer:doctor
when heard_lie:scav.chemist
topic "Ask about the chemist's in town."
prio reaction
once
voice plain

node start
  say "The chemist's? I cleared it myself, Day 3. Every shelf. Whoever told you otherwise wanted a tin more than you did." ~truth:scav.chemist
  > @thanks "Good to know." -> hub

conv wanderer.doctor.back_room
for wanderer:doctor
when heard_lie:halcyon.back_room
topic "Ask about Halcyon's volunteers."
prio reaction
once
voice plain

node start
  say "The two who don't walk out? There's a room at the back of the lab. A chair by every bed and someone with a clipboard in it." ~truth:halcyon.back_room
  say "They're not cruel. They write everything down. That's worse, some days."
  > @thanks "Thank you for telling me." -> hub
